window.__SLIDES&&window.__SLIDES('g1',{"s":["<section id=\"g1-tldr\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:28px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">LLM robot teams · 2021–2025</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">LLM robot teams: from talking to guarantees</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px\">\n<div style=\"width:880px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:28px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Background · before the series</p><ul style=\"font-size:26px;line-height:1.3;color:#16212F\"><li><b>One-robot LLM planners</b> · SayCan and Inner Monologue let an LLM pick skills for one robot (cited by RoCo, KnowNo).</li><li><b>Embodied helping</b> · Watch-And-Help (guest, from the Embodied helpers tree) gave the C-WAH task and MHP planner that CoELA, CoTS reuse.</li><li><b>Conformal prediction</b> · Vovk et al. gave answer sets with set odds; Kumar et al. used them for LLM multiple choice (KnowNo).</li><li><b>Dialogue first</b> · CoELA and RoCo gave each robot an LLM that chats (cited by Centralized vs not, CoTS).</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Problem</p><p style=\"font-size:26px;line-height:1.3;color:#16212F\">A team of robots must plan one task from language, each with its own view, while messages cost LLM calls and an LLM can be wrong.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Idea</p><p style=\"font-size:26px;line-height:1.3;color:#16212F\">Give each robot an LLM that talks; then fix its limits: central planning for scale, tree search for better plans, conformal sets for guarantees.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<img src=\"assets/img/g1_tldr.webp\" alt=\"Lineage of the key papers in this work tree, drawn by year with arrows from parent to child\" style=\"width:736px;height:260px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3;color:#5B6472\">Solid arrows: inheritance. Watch-And-Help is a guest; COMBO has none. White pills are guests: papers whose home is another tree, included because they sit on a lineage here.</p>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;background:#EFEBE0;border-radius:16px;padding:18px 24px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Terms</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\"><b style=\"color:#2D2D71\">DMAS / CMAS</b> · decentralized (LLM per robot) vs centralized (one LLM)</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\"><b style=\"color:#2D2D71\">Conformal prediction</b> · a set that holds the answer with set odds</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\"><b style=\"color:#2D2D71\">MCTS</b> · tree search that tries and scores many plans</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\"><b style=\"color:#2D2D71\">Oracle perception</b> · agents get true object info, no vision errors</p></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">LLM planning for robot teams</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">8 papers (1 guests) · 2021–2025 · CoELA → KnowNo → Watch-And-Help</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"g1-assume\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:28px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">LLM robot teams · Assumptions</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">LLM robot teams assume cooperation in simulation</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px\"><div style=\"display:flex;gap:32px;align-items:flex-start;padding-bottom:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"width:500px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25;color:#2D2D71\">Simulation first</p><p style=\"flex:1;font-size:26px;line-height:1.3;color:#16212F\">Mostly simulated; KnowNo, RoCo, COMBO add small real-robot runs (COMBO 4/5); C-WAH inherits VirtualHome.</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:32px;align-items:flex-start;padding-bottom:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"width:500px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25;color:#2D2D71\">One shared goal</p><p style=\"flex:1;font-size:26px;line-height:1.3;color:#16212F\">All robots are cooperative and know the same task; none faces an adversary or hidden goal.</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:32px;align-items:flex-start;padding-bottom:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"width:500px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25;color:#2D2D71\">Text or clean state</p><p style=\"flex:1;font-size:26px;line-height:1.3;color:#16212F\">Most planners get text or oracle state; CoELA and COMBO use egocentric RGB-D.</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:32px;align-items:flex-start;padding-bottom:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"width:500px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25;color:#2D2D71\">Few robots</p><p style=\"flex:1;font-size:26px;line-height:1.3;color:#16212F\">Mostly two; Centralized vs not scales to 32 (BoxNet), Conformal MRP to 15, COMBO to 4.</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:32px;align-items:flex-start;padding-bottom:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"width:500px;font-size:28px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25;color:#2D2D71\">Costly language</p><p style=\"flex:1;font-size:26px;line-height:1.3;color:#16212F\">Every message is an LLM query; Centralized vs not relaxes the cost with a central planner.</p></div></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:20px;align-items:center\"><div style=\"width:760px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#E3E3F7;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Builds on</p><p style=\"font-size:26px;line-height:1.3\">One-robot LLM planners (SayCan, Inner Monologue), Watch-And-Help&#x27;s household tasks, and conformal prediction.</p></div><svg width=\"48\" height=\"30\" viewBox=\"0 0 48 30\" style=\"flex:none;display:block;\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M0,9.0 L28.799999999999997,9.0 L28.799999999999997,0 L48.0,15.0 L28.799999999999997,30.0 L28.799999999999997,21.0 L0,21.0 Z\" fill=\"#2D2D71\"/></svg><div style=\"width:816px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#E3E3F7;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">So the series achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:26px;line-height:1.3\">LLM teams (CoELA, RoCo), scaling (Centralized vs not), better plans (CoTS), a success guarantee (KnowNo, Conformal MRP).</p></div></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">LLM planning for robot teams</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">8 papers (1 guests) · 2021–2025 · CoELA → KnowNo → Watch-And-Help</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"g1-method\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">LLM robot teams · Evolution</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">Talk first, then search, guarantee or leave text</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"background:#E3E3F7;border-radius:16px;padding:18px 32px\"><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.35\">CoELA and RoCo make LLMs talk (on WAH&#x27;s tasks for CoELA); later papers repair talk (central planner), plan better (tree search) or guarantee success.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px\">\n<img src=\"assets/img/g1_method.webp\" alt=\"Lineage of every paper in the work tree by year, arrows from parent to child\" style=\"width:1664px;height:470px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3;color:#5B6472\">Each arrow points from a paper to the paper that builds on it. Dark pills mark the key papers. White pills are guests: papers whose home is another tree, included because they sit on a lineage here. Papers without an arrow are tied to the series only by baseline comparisons.</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">LLM planning for robot teams</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">8 papers (1 guests) · 2021–2025 · CoELA → KnowNo → Watch-And-Help</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"g1-stages\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:28px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">LLM robot teams · Stages</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">The series unfolds in three stages</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:16px;align-items:stretch\"><div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:18px;background:#FFFEFB;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;border-top:8px solid #C8651B;border-radius:16px;padding:28px 32px\"><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:32px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.15;color:#C8651B\">1 · Per-robot LLM dialogue</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3;color:#5B6472\">2021–2024</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;background:#E3E3F7;border:2px solid #2D2D71;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px\">Watch-And-Help</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;background:#E3E3F7;border:2px solid #2D2D71;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px\">CoELA</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;background:#E3E3F7;border:2px solid #2D2D71;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px\">RoCo</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;background:#E3E3F7;border:2px solid #2D2D71;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px\">Centralized vs not</p></div><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.35\">WAH: C-WAH task and MHP planner. CoELA: five modules, LLMs write messages. RoCo: dialogue plus checks. Centralized vs not: central planner.</p></div><svg width=\"40\" height=\"28\" viewBox=\"0 0 40 28\" style=\"flex:none;display:block;\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M0,8.4 L24.0,8.4 L24.0,0 L40.0,14.0 L24.0,28.0 L24.0,19.599999999999998 L0,19.599999999999998 Z\" fill=\"#2D2D71\"/></svg><div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:18px;background:#FFFEFB;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;border-top:8px solid #3E6FD9;border-radius:16px;padding:28px 32px\"><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:32px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.15;color:#3E6FD9\">2 · Better or safer plans</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3;color:#5B6472\">2023–2025</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;background:#E3E3F7;border:2px solid #2D2D71;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px\">CoTS</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;background:#E3E3F7;border:2px solid #2D2D71;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px\">KnowNo</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;background:#E3E3F7;border:2px solid #2D2D71;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px\">Conformal MRP</p></div><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.35\">CoTS: tree search over plans. KnowNo: ask a human if the conformal set is not 1. Conformal MRP: that, per robot in a team.</p></div><svg width=\"40\" height=\"28\" viewBox=\"0 0 40 28\" style=\"flex:none;display:block;\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M0,8.4 L24.0,8.4 L24.0,0 L40.0,14.0 L24.0,28.0 L24.0,19.599999999999998 L0,19.599999999999998 Z\" fill=\"#2D2D71\"/></svg><div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:18px;background:#FFFEFB;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;border-top:8px solid #8E4FC9;border-radius:16px;padding:28px 32px\"><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:32px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.15;color:#8E4FC9\">3 · Beyond text planning</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3;color:#5B6472\">2025</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:10px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:500;background:#E3E3F7;border:2px solid #2D2D71;border-radius:999px;padding:6px 16px\">COMBO</p></div><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.35\">COMBO: a video world model composes each agent&#x27;s action; VLMs propose, track intents and search. It only compares against CoELA.</p></div></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">LLM planning for robot teams</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">8 papers (1 guests) · 2021–2025 · CoELA → KnowNo → Watch-And-Help</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"g1-s01\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">LLM robot teams · Watch-And-Help 2021 · 1 of 8 · Guest</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">Watch-And-Help: the helping task CoELA and CoTS reuse</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:900px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Starts from</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Home: Embodied helpers tree. Builds on VirtualHome, Theory of Mind goal inference, MCTS and regression planning. Here: source of C-WAH and MHP.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Assumes</p><ul style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\"><li>One demo, goal hidden at test; symbolic partial views</li><li>Alice is a human-like planner or a real human</li><li>Five household activities; no direct communication</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Adds</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">The Watch-Help challenge, VirtualHome-Social, and an MCTS plus regression-planning hierarchical planner (HP, later MHP) CoELA and CoTS reuse.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Place in the tree</p><img src=\"assets/img/g1_s01.webp\" alt=\"Papers this one builds on at left, this paper in the middle, papers that build on it at right\" style=\"width:716px;height:108px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\"></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px;background:#E3E3F7;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 24px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Next in the series</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\">CoELA extends it into C-WAH and adopts its MHP baseline; CoTS tests on C-WAH.</p></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#E3E3F7;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.3\">Goal inference precision 0.85 / recall 0.96 (VirtualHome-Social, test-1); planning Bobs speed Alice up.</p></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Watch-And-Help: A Challenge for Social Perception and Human-AI Collaboration</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">Puig et al. · ICLR 2021</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"g1-s02\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">LLM robot teams · KnowNo 2023 · 2 of 8</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">KnowNo: ask a human only when the LLM is unsure</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:900px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Starts from</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Outside works: conformal prediction, MCQA scoring (Kumar et al.), SayCan and Inner Monologue. No parent in this tree.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Assumes</p><ul style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\"><li>Calibration data drawn i.i.d. (N=400)</li><li>A faithful human helper; one robot</li><li>Scene fully described in text; actions executable</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Adds</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Poses planning as multiple choice; conformal prediction keeps a set of likely options; the robot asks only if more than one remains.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Place in the tree</p><img src=\"assets/img/g1_s02.webp\" alt=\"Papers this one builds on at left, this paper in the middle, papers that build on it at right\" style=\"width:716px;height:62px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\"></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px;background:#E3E3F7;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 24px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Next in the series</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\">Conformal MRP generalises its conformal help-asking from one robot to distributed teams.</p></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#E3E3F7;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.3\">10-24% less human help than baselines at the target success rate (tabletop sim, UR5 arm, kitchen arm).</p></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Robots That Ask For Help: Uncertainty Alignment for Large Language Model Planners</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">Ren et al. · CoRL 2023</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"g1-s03\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">LLM robot teams · CoELA 2024 · 3 of 8</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">CoELA: modular LLM agents that plan, talk and cooperate</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:900px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Starts from</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Reuses Watch-And-Help&#x27;s C-WAH task and MHP planner. Outside: Laird, Song, Huang. Cites RoCo as related work.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Assumes</p><ul style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\"><li>Decentralized agents, one shared goal; messages cost time</li><li>Two agents (AI or human partner); noise-free messages</li><li>Egocentric RGB-D with a trained Mask-RCNN; GPT-4 by API</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Adds</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Five modules (perception, memory, communication, planning, execution); the LLMs only write messages and pick high-level plans.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Place in the tree</p><img src=\"assets/img/g1_s03.webp\" alt=\"Papers this one builds on at left, this paper in the middle, papers that build on it at right\" style=\"width:716px;height:200px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\"></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px;background:#E3E3F7;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 24px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Next in the series</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\">Centralized vs not builds on its dialogue; CoTS builds on it; COMBO only compares.</p></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#E3E3F7;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.3\">TDW-MAT transport rate 0.71 vs 0.43 alone (+39% EI) with two GPT-4 CoELAs; C-WAH steps 57 vs 111 alone.</p></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Building Cooperative Embodied Agents Modularly with Large Language Models</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">Zhang et al. · ICLR 2024</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"g1-s04\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">LLM robot teams · RoCo 2024 · 4 of 8</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">RoCo: robots debate in text, then a planner moves them</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:900px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Starts from</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Outside works: SayCan and Inner Monologue, LLM dialog prompting, RRT motion planning. No parent in this tree.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Assumes</p><ul style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\"><li>Cooperative robots, one GPT-4 agent each, asymmetric views</li><li>Accurate perception (oracle state in sim); open-loop run</li><li>Hand-written text interfaces for each task</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Adds</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Per-robot LLM dialog, then a checked sub-task plan (parsing, IK, collisions) fed back on failure, then a multi-arm RRT planner.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Place in the tree</p><img src=\"assets/img/g1_s04.webp\" alt=\"Papers this one builds on at left, this paper in the middle, papers that build on it at right\" style=\"width:716px;height:200px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\"></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px;background:#E3E3F7;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 24px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Next in the series</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\">Centralized vs not takes its per-robot dialogue as the starting framework; CoTS compares against it.</p></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#E3E3F7;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.3\">RoCoBench success 0.44-0.95 over six tasks (20 runs each); dialog beats the oracle central plan on Sort Cubes and Move Rope.</p></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">RoCo: Dialectic Multi-Robot Collaboration with Large Language Models</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">Mandi et al. · ICRA 2024</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"g1-s05\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">LLM robot teams · Centralized vs not 2024 · 5 of 8</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">Centralized vs not: a central LLM with local checks</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:900px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Starts from</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Builds on CoELA and RoCo: takes their per-robot LLM dialogue (DMAS) as the starting framework and adds central and hybrid variants.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Assumes</p><ul style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\"><li>Every LLM knows the full environment and all robot skills</li><li>Hand-built text interface; cooperative robots</li><li>GPT-4&#x27;s 8,192-token limit; 3,500-token state-action history</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Adds</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Compares DMAS, CMAS and two hybrids; the best, HMAS-2, keeps one central planner and lets each acting robot&#x27;s LLM give feedback.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Place in the tree</p><img src=\"assets/img/g1_s05.webp\" alt=\"Papers this one builds on at left, this paper in the middle, papers that build on it at right\" style=\"width:716px;height:108px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\"></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px;background:#E3E3F7;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 24px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Next in the series</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\">Conformal MRP only compares against it; no member builds on it.</p></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#E3E3F7;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.3\">Warehouse success 62.5% (HMAS-2) vs 15.0% (CMAS) and 0% (DMAS), mean of 40 runs; BoxLift 100.0%.</p></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Scalable Multi-Robot Collaboration with Large Language Models: Centralized or Decentralized Systems?</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">Chen et al. · ICRA 2024</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"g1-s06\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">LLM robot teams · COMBO 2025 · 6 of 8</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">COMBO: plan with a compositional video world model</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:900px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Starts from</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">No parent in this tree: builds on composable diffusion, the AVDC video model and VLP tree search; only compares against CoELA.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Assumes</p><ul style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\"><li>Decentralized agents with egocentric partial RGBD views</li><li>Teammates are unknown scripted policies; simulator data</li><li>Slow, compute-heavy tree search is acceptable</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Adds</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">A video world model composes one prediction per agent&#x27;s action; VLMs propose actions, guess teammates&#x27; intents and score futures in tree search.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Place in the tree</p><img src=\"assets/img/g1_s06.webp\" alt=\"Papers this one builds on at left, this paper in the middle, papers that build on it at right\" style=\"width:716px;height:62px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\"></div>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#E3E3F7;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.3\">100% success in 17.5 steps on TDW-Game (cooperator 1) vs 55% in 28.4 for fine-tuned LLaVA; 20 episodes.</p></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">COMBO: Compositional World Models for Embodied Multi-Agent Cooperation</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">Zhang et al. · ICLR 2025</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"g1-s07\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">LLM robot teams · Conformal MRP 2025 · 7 of 8</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">Conformal MRP: team LLM plans with a success guarantee</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:900px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Starts from</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Builds on KnowNo: generalises its conformal help-asking to distributed teams. Compares against Centralized vs not&#x27;s CMAS and DMAS.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Assumes</p><ul style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\"><li>Skills execute without error; guarantee covers LLM mistakes</li><li>Test missions i.i.d. with calibration; scene known and static</li><li>Faithful human helper; homogeneous robots, known states</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Adds</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Robots choose actions one by one; each LLM answers a multiple-choice question; a conformal set means act if one action, else ask a human.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Place in the tree</p><img src=\"assets/img/g1_s07.webp\" alt=\"Papers this one builds on at left, this paper in the middle, papers that build on it at right\" style=\"width:716px;height:200px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\"></div>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#E3E3F7;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.3\">94.59% success at a 90% target (AI2-THOR, GPT-3.5, 110 scenarios); 2-robot help 29% vs 88% for a centralized version (Llama 2).</p></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Probabilistically Correct Language-based Multi-Robot Planning using Conformal Prediction</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">Wang et al. · RA-L 2025</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"g1-s08\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">LLM robot teams · CoTS 2025 · 8 of 8</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">CoTS: agents search a tree of dialogues for a team plan</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:48px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:900px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:30px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Starts from</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">Builds on CoELA: swaps its planner for MCTS-style tree search. Reuses Watch-And-Help&#x27;s C-WAH environment. Compares RoCo.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Assumes</p><ul style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\"><li>Two decentralized agents with own LLMs: a planner and a critic</li><li>Plans scored by the LLM (no environment rollout)</li><li>Strong LLM; CoELA&#x27;s perception, memory, execution reused</li></ul></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Adds</p><p style=\"font-size:28px;line-height:1.3\">A planner agent drafts plans, a critic scores them; MCTS grows branches by UCT; an evaluator re-plans only when the plan stops fitting.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Place in the tree</p><img src=\"assets/img/g1_s08.webp\" alt=\"Papers this one builds on at left, this paper in the middle, papers that build on it at right\" style=\"width:716px;height:154px;object-fit:contain;border-radius:12px;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;background:#FFFFFF\"></div>\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#E3E3F7;border-radius:16px;padding:16px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Achieves</p><p style=\"font-size:30px;line-height:1.3\">TDW-MAT (GPT-4, oracle perception) 93% vs CoELA 85% transport rate (+9.41%); C-WAH symbolic 49 vs 57 steps.</p></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">Collaborative Tree Search for Enhancing Embodied Multi-Agent Collaboration</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">Zu et al. · CVPR 2025</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"g1-eval\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">LLM robot teams · Evaluation</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">Each paper is tested on its own benchmark</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;gap:32px;align-items:flex-start\">\n<div style=\"width:560px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:20px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px;background:#FFFEFB;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;border-radius:16px;padding:22px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472\">Benchmarks and baselines</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\">LLM-team papers use simulators: TDW-MAT and C-WAH (CoELA, CoTS), RoCoBench, BoxNet and Warehouse, AI2-THOR.</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\">KnowNo adds UR5 and kitchen arms; COMBO uses TDW-Game and TDW-Cook.</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.3\">CoELA and CoTS share TDW-MAT and C-WAH (from Watch-And-Help); CoTS copies CoELA&#x27;s numbers.</p></div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;background:#E3E3F7;border-radius:16px;padding:18px 28px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">Reading</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.35\">Benchmarks, metrics and baselines differ: never rank rows; read each as that paper&#x27;s own gain over its baselines.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px;background:#FFFEFB;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;border-radius:16px;padding:20px 32px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#5B6472;padding-bottom:4px\">Headline result of each paper</p><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0px;padding:5px 0px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.25\"><b style=\"color:#2D2D71\">Watch-And-Help</b> · <span style=\"color:#5B6472\">VirtualHome-Social, test-1 (100 tasks)</span></p><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25\">goal inference precision 0.85 / recall 0.96</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0px;padding:5px 0px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.25\"><b style=\"color:#2D2D71\">KnowNo</b> · <span style=\"color:#5B6472\">Tabletop sim, UR5 arm, kitchen arm</span></p><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25\">10-24% less help at the target success rate</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0px;padding:5px 0px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.25\"><b style=\"color:#2D2D71\">CoELA</b> · <span style=\"color:#5B6472\">TDW-MAT</span></p><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25\">transport rate 0.71 vs 0.43 alone</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0px;padding:5px 0px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.25\"><b style=\"color:#2D2D71\">RoCo</b> · <span style=\"color:#5B6472\">RoCoBench, 6 tasks, 20 runs each</span></p><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25\">success 0.44-0.95 (dialog)</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0px;padding:5px 0px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.25\"><b style=\"color:#2D2D71\">Centralized vs not</b> · <span style=\"color:#5B6472\">Warehouse, 40 runs</span></p><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25\">success 62.5% (HMAS-2) vs 15.0% (CMAS)</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0px;padding:5px 0px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.25\"><b style=\"color:#2D2D71\">CoTS</b> · <span style=\"color:#5B6472\">TDW-MAT (GPT-4, oracle perception)</span></p><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25\">transport rate 93% vs CoELA 85%</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0px;padding:5px 0px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.25\"><b style=\"color:#2D2D71\">Conformal MRP</b> · <span style=\"color:#5B6472\">AI2-THOR, 110 scenarios</span></p><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25\">94.59% success at a 90% target</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0px;padding:5px 0px;border-bottom:1px solid #DDD8CB\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;line-height:1.25\"><b style=\"color:#2D2D71\">COMBO</b> · <span style=\"color:#5B6472\">TDW-Game, cooperator 1</span></p><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.25\">100% success in 17.5 steps (20 episodes)</p></div></div>\n</div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">LLM planning for robot teams</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">8 papers (1 guests) · 2021–2025 · CoELA → KnowNo → Watch-And-Help</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>","<section id=\"g1-open\" style=\"background:#FAF8F3;color:#16212F;font-family:'IBM Plex Sans', Arial, sans-serif;padding:96px 128px 160px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:28px\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:4px\">\n<p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;color:#2D2D71\">LLM robot teams · Open questions</p>\n<h2 style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:56px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.1;color:#16212F\">What the series still leaves open</h2>\n</div>\n<div style=\"display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:24px\"><div style=\"display:flex;gap:32px;align-items:center;background:#FFFEFB;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;border-left:8px solid #2D2D71;border-radius:16px;padding:28px 36px\"><p style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:64px;font-weight:600;line-height:1;color:#2D2D71;width:56px\">1</p><p style=\"flex:1;font-size:32px;line-height:1.35\">Mostly simulated, small test sets (CoELA 24 and 10 episodes, COMBO 20); C-WAH tasks are symbolic.</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:32px;align-items:center;background:#FFFEFB;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;border-left:8px solid #2D2D71;border-radius:16px;padding:28px 36px\"><p style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:64px;font-weight:600;line-height:1;color:#2D2D71;width:56px\">2</p><p style=\"flex:1;font-size:32px;line-height:1.35\">Each message is an LLM query: LLM teams are slow and costly; HMAS-2 needs more calls than CMAS.</p></div><div style=\"display:flex;gap:32px;align-items:center;background:#FFFEFB;border:1px solid #DDD8CB;border-left:8px solid #2D2D71;border-radius:16px;padding:28px 36px\"><p style=\"font-family:'Source Serif 4', Georgia, serif;font-size:64px;font-weight:600;line-height:1;color:#2D2D71;width:56px\">3</p><p style=\"flex:1;font-size:32px;line-height:1.35\">Guarantees assume error-free skills and i.i.d. calibration (Conformal MRP, KnowNo); COMBO is slow.</p></div></div>\n<div style=\"position:absolute;left:128px;bottom:56px;width:1664px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:2px\"><p style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:600;color:#16212F\">LLM planning for robot teams</p><p style=\"font-size:24px;color:#5B6472\">8 papers (1 guests) · 2021–2025 · CoELA → KnowNo → Watch-And-Help</p></div>\n\n</section>\n\n</section>"],"n":["Members (year): Watch-And-Help 2021 (GUEST), KnowNo 2023, CoELA 2024, RoCo 2024, Centralized vs not 2024, COMBO 2025, Conformal MRP 2025, CoTS 2025. Edges: 12, of which 4 are method inheritance (kind 0), 2 are component reuse (kind 1) and 6 are citations or comparisons (kind 2). Inheritance: CoELA -&gt; Centralized vs not and RoCo -&gt; Centralized vs not (per-robot LLM dialogue is the starting framework; adds central and hybrid variants); KnowNo -&gt; Conformal MRP (conformal multiple-choice planning and help-seeking, made distributed); CoELA -&gt; CoTS (keeps most modules, planner replaced by tree search). Guest edges (kind 1, solid): Watch-And-Help -&gt; CoELA (C-WAH extends WAH; MHP planner adopted) and Watch-And-Help -&gt; CoTS (C-WAH reused as benchmark). Watch-And-Help is a guest from the Embodied helpers and benchmarks tree; it is a non-LLM benchmark paper, kept because two members reuse its task and planner. Comparisons only: CoELA -&gt; COMBO (baseline); RoCo -&gt; CoTS (baseline); Centralized vs not -&gt; Conformal MRP (baseline, appendix A); CoELA, RoCo -&gt; Conformal MRP (related-work citation); RoCo -&gt; CoELA (related-work list; I checked: no reuse). So COMBO has no solid edge: it joins the line by topic and by comparison, and the slides say so. Two seeds: CoELA and RoCo (dialogue) and KnowNo (conformal help-asking). Their descendants are the three solid chains. KnowNo is a one-robot method (tags: single robot asks a human); it is here because of its descendant. Background: from the members&#x27; own related work (SayCan, Inner Monologue, Vovk et al., Kumar et al.); the selection of works is mine. The shared problem and idea are my synthesis, not a claim by any one paper. Uncertain: venue years for RoCo, Centralized vs not and Conformal MRP come from file names, not the PDFs. The old tree t6 also contained helping papers (NOPA, Smart Help, CHAIC, Co-GAIL) that are now in other trees; WAH returns as a guest.","Assumptions shared across the line (my synthesis from each paper&#x27;s assume slide; papers rarely list assumptions). Simulation: Watch-And-Help (VirtualHome-Social, symbolic partial views; guest), CoELA (TDW-MAT, C-WAH), RoCo (MuJoCo RoCoBench; also a UR5E arm with a human, 10 runs per setup), KnowNo (tabletop sim plus UR5 and kitchen hardware), Centralized vs not (2D and PyBullet), COMBO (TDW; 4/5 real robot runs in the appendix), Conformal MRP (AI2-THOR), CoTS (TDW-MAT, C-WAH). Shared goal and cooperation: all robots are cooperative; LLM-team papers give all agents the same task description. Conformal MRP and KnowNo assume a faithful human who picks the right option when asked. Observations: RoCo, Centralized vs not, KnowNo, Conformal MRP rely on accurate or text-described state; CoELA and COMBO use egocentric RGB-D (CoELA with a trained Mask-RCNN); CoTS also tests without oracle perception, borrowed from CoELA. Team size: mostly two agents. Counts: Centralized vs not 4-32 robots (BoxNet) and 4-10 (Warehouse, BoxLift); Conformal MRP 1-15; COMBO 2-4; CoELA, CoTS two. Cost: every message is an LLM query (CoELA, RoCo); Centralized vs not gives full knowledge to each LLM and meets the token limit; Conformal MRP assumes error-free skills and i.i.d. calibration data. Where a later member relaxes an assumption: Centralized vs not replaces per-robot talk by a central planner; Conformal MRP adds a success guarantee; CoTS adds long-term plan search. Achieved (numbers are not comparable): see the evaluation slide.","Three groups, ordered roughly by time, not a strict chain. Per-robot LLM dialogue (2021-2024): Watch-And-Help (guest, 2021: the C-WAH task and MHP planner that CoELA adopts, kind 1; no LLM); CoELA (five modules; LLMs write messages and pick plans); RoCo (per-robot dialog, validated sub-task plan, multi-arm RRT); Centralized vs not (kind 0 from both: compares DMAS, CMAS, HMAS-1, HMAS-2; HMAS-2 keeps a central planner with local LLM feedback). Better or safer plans (2023-2025): CoTS (kind 0 from CoELA: planner replaced by MCTS over dialogue plans plus a plan-update evaluator); KnowNo (conformal multiple-choice planning, ask if set &gt; 1) and Conformal MRP (kind 0 from KnowNo: per-robot conformal sets, act or ask). KnowNo is placed here because of its descendant; it is a one-robot method. Beyond text planning (2025): COMBO (compositional video world model with VLM proposals and tree search; baseline link to CoELA only). Why this order: Watch-And-Help predates the others and supplies the environment; the edge notes say CoELA and RoCo are the starting framework of Centralized vs not; CoTS keeps most CoELA modules; Conformal MRP generalises KnowNo. Numbers on method details: KnowNo N=400 calibration examples; COMBO P=B=D=3; CoTS UCT selection with LLM reward in 0-1. Uncertain: the three-group split is my editorial summary; CoTS&#x27;s threshold and COMBO&#x27;s k are not stated in the notes.","Three groups, ordered roughly by time, not a strict chain. Per-robot LLM dialogue (2021-2024): Watch-And-Help (guest, 2021: the C-WAH task and MHP planner that CoELA adopts, kind 1; no LLM); CoELA (five modules; LLMs write messages and pick plans); RoCo (per-robot dialog, validated sub-task plan, multi-arm RRT); Centralized vs not (kind 0 from both: compares DMAS, CMAS, HMAS-1, HMAS-2; HMAS-2 keeps a central planner with local LLM feedback). Better or safer plans (2023-2025): CoTS (kind 0 from CoELA: planner replaced by MCTS over dialogue plans plus a plan-update evaluator); KnowNo (conformal multiple-choice planning, ask if set &gt; 1) and Conformal MRP (kind 0 from KnowNo: per-robot conformal sets, act or ask). KnowNo is placed here because of its descendant; it is a one-robot method. Beyond text planning (2025): COMBO (compositional video world model with VLM proposals and tree search; baseline link to CoELA only). Why this order: Watch-And-Help predates the others and supplies the environment; the edge notes say CoELA and RoCo are the starting framework of Centralized vs not; CoTS keeps most CoELA modules; Conformal MRP generalises KnowNo. Numbers on method details: KnowNo N=400 calibration examples; COMBO P=B=D=3; CoTS UCT selection with LLM reward in 0-1. Uncertain: the three-group split is my editorial summary; CoTS&#x27;s threshold and COMBO&#x27;s k are not stated in the notes.","Watch-And-Help (Puig, Shu, Li, Wang, Liao, Tenenbaum, Fidler, Torralba; ICLR 2021). GUEST in this tree; home tree: Embodied helpers and benchmarks. It is here because two members reuse its artefacts; it is not an LLM paper and does not use language. Edges used (both kind 1, component reuse): CoELA -&gt; WAH (C-WAH is &#x27;extended from the Watch-And-Help Challenge&#x27; on VirtualHome-Social, adding communication; the MCTS-based Hierarchical Planner MHP is &#x27;adopted from the strongest baseline in the original Watch-And-Help Challenge&#x27;); CoTS -&gt; WAH (C-WAH test environment, reused as a CoTS benchmark; CoTS&#x27; MHP baseline is cited to a different paper than WAH in its text, so I did not count it). No edge to COMBO: COMBO only contrasts itself with WAH as work that does not model world dynamics (not counted). Start (paper&#x27;s related work): activity recognition for short actions; Theory of Mind in toy 2D grids (Baker et al.); lab-based human-robot help; game-like multi-agent platforms; VirtualHome for one agent. Assumptions (Sec. 3-5.1, App. A-B): Bob sees Alice do the task once (ground-truth goal shown only in training); goals are 2-8 predicates over 30 types in five activities; training 1011 tasks, two test sets of 100; helping home differs from the demo home; symbolic scene graph, partial view limited to the same room and open containers; ground-truth object states, not pixels; Alice plans from her beliefs with MCTS plus regression planning; limit 250 steps. Communication and online goal inference are left as future work. Method: Transformer plus LSTM predicts the count of each of 30 predicates; Bob is hierarchical: a high-level subgoal chooser (MCTS = HP, RL = Hybrid, both learned = HRL) and a low-level planner. Numbers (Sec. 5.3): goal inference test-1 precision 0.85 / recall 0.96 (last observation only 0.79 / 0.75; chance 0.08 / 0.09); test-2 0.68 / 0.64. Random goals (HP_RG) cause conflicts in 40% of episodes. HRL no better than Random. Test-2: HP 88.6% success, speedup 0.21 (Alice alone 95.4%, which the notes call odd). Caveats: per-method test-1 success and speedup are only in Fig. 5 plots; headline chosen as the Watch-stage numbers (no single headline in the paper). CoELA and CoTS use C-WAH with a modified task set (10 test episodes) and steps, so their numbers are not comparable with WAH&#x27;s.","KnowNo (Ren et al., CoRL 2023; venue from PDF metadata). Edge used: parent of Conformal MRP (kind 0: builds on KnowNo&#x27;s conformal-prediction multiple-choice planner and help-seeking, generalising it to distributed teams). No parent in the tree. The tags say a single robot asks a human, so the lane fit is only by descendant. Start: SayCan never asks; Inner Monologue asks with extensive prompting; neither ties asking to a success level. Conformal prediction (Vovk) was used for LLM multiple-choice QA only (Kumar et al.). Assumptions (Secs 2-4, Discussion): scenarios sampled i.i.d. for calibration (N=400, delta=0.01); the human helps faithfully; objects fully grounded in text and actions executable; one robot and one supervisor; coverage holds whether or not LLM scores are calibrated. Method: LLM drafts four options plus &#x27;not listed&#x27;; next-token probability of letters A-E gives scores; nonconformity score 1 - f(correct); quantile from calibration; keep options above the threshold; one option means act, else ask showing only those. Multi-step case calibrates at sequence level. Numbers: help reduced 10-24% vs baselines (paper&#x27;s own summary). Hardware tabletop (Table 1, 50 trials, eps=0.25): plan success 0.76, task success 0.74, help per step 0.58 vs Simple Set 0.72. Mobile kitchen (Table 2, eps=0.15): help 0.67 vs 0.81, task success 0.76 vs 0.75; No Help 0.51. Uncertain: kitchen trial count not found; Fig. 3/4 curves have no printed numbers; the builds-on list is partly my selection.","CoELA (Zhang, Du et al., ICLR 2024). Edges in this tree: child of Watch-And-Help (kind 1: C-WAH is extended from WAH, MHP baseline adopted from it); parent of Centralized vs not (kind 0, with RoCo: treats per-robot LLM dialogue as starting framework), parent of CoTS (kind 0: keeps most modules, replaces the planner with tree search plus extended memory), parent of COMBO (kind 2, reimplemented with oracle perception as baseline); child of RoCo by citation only (kind 2: RoCo sits in a related-work list on grounding communication; no reuse). Conformal MRP cites it only in a list (kind 2). Start: cognitive architectures (Laird, Langley) and single-agent LLM planners (Song 2022, Huang 2022a); earlier embodied cooperation work neglected communication (paper&#x27;s characterization; not verified). Assumptions (Sec. 3, 5.1, App. A-B): Dec-POMDP-COM, shared team reward; noise-free broadcast and two agents in all experiments; sending a message costs time; 512x512 RGB-D, Mask-RCNN fine-tuned on 53K images (81.4 mAP@50); the LLM picks from a list of high-level plans, execution is hand-coded; GPT-4 via API. Numbers: Table 1 (TDW-MAT, transport rate, no oracle perception): RHP 0.43; RHP+RHP 0.61; RHP+CoELA 0.69; CoELA+CoELA GPT-4 0.71 (+39%), LLAMA-2 0.53, CoLLAMA 0.70. With oracle perception GPT-4 0.85 (+41%). Table 2 (C-WAH steps, symbolic): MHP 111; MHP+MHP 75; MHP+CoELA 59; CoELA+CoELA 57 (+49%); visual 141, 103, 94, 92. Human study (8 subjects): trust 6.3 vs 4.7 without communication (p=0.0003). Caveats: CoELA numbers are single runs, baselines 5 runs; test sets of 24 and 10 episodes. Footnote experiment dates inconsistent (2023.9 vs 2023.5). Ablation Fig. 4c only as a chart. Guest link: C-WAH is built on Watch-And-Help (home: Embodied helpers tree); the WAH numbers (goal inference 0.85/0.96) are a different task and are not comparable with CoELA&#x27;s steps.","RoCo (Mandi, Jain, Song; Columbia; PDF is arXiv v1 in the CoRL 2023 template; venue ICRA 2024 taken from the file name). Edges: parent of Centralized vs not (kind 0: treats RoCo-style per-robot dialogue (DMAS) as starting framework). Compared as baseline by CoTS (kind 2); cited as an LLM-per-robot planner without guarantees by Conformal MRP (kind 2); in CoELA&#x27;s related work (kind 2). No parent in the tree. Start: single-robot LLM planners (SayCan, Inner Monologue), LLM plus task-and-motion planning (Text2Motion, AutoTAMP), dialog prompting outside robotics. Assumptions (Secs 2, 3.1, 7): N cooperative robots; each has its own LLM agent; asymmetric observations in 3 of 6 tasks; hand-written description and parsing functions; accurate perception (oracle state), open-loop trajectories, every message is an LLM query. GPT-4 for all main results. Method: dialog until one agent summarizes (allowed only after everyone spoke once); validation chain: parsing, task constraints, IK, collisions, waypoints; failures return to dialog; a centralized multi-arm RRT planner executes. Numbers (Table 2, success over 20 runs, Dialog / oracle Central Plan): Pack Grocery 0.44 / 0.82; Arrange Cabinet 0.75 / 0.90; Sweep Floor 0.95 / 1.00; Make Sandwich 0.80 / 0.96; Sort Cubes 0.93 / 0.70; Move Rope 0.65 / 0.50. The 0.75 mean is MY average (the paper reports none). Real UR5E arm with a human (10 runs each): 9/10 and 8/10 with an oracle human, 7/10 and 6/10 with an imperfect one; bottleneck is OWL-ViT detection errors. Uncertain: zero-shot vs few-shot wording; Fig. 4 waypoint result is qualitative only.","Centralized vs not (Chen, Arkin, Zhang, Roy, Fan; arXiv v2 Mar 2024; venue ICRA 2024 taken from the file name). Edges: child of CoELA and of RoCo (both kind 0; its text calls DMAS &#x27;the framework used in previous works [10], [11]&#x27; and says two or three robots were the scope of prior work). Compared as baseline by Conformal MRP (kind 2, appendix A: CMAS and DMAS). Problem: with many robots every extra LLM adds to the context, nearing token limits and diluting information; prior work handled 2 or 3 robots. Assumptions (Secs II-IV): each LLM agent has full knowledge of the environment and each robot&#x27;s skills; manual prompt and parsing functions plus a rules-based syntax verifier; cooperative tasks; incremental planning with a state-action history (sliding window up to 3,500 tokens; GPT-4 8,192). Failure on token overflow, no consensus, syntax loop, too many iterations or collision. All simulation. Method: DMAS (one LLM per robot), CMAS (one central LLM), HMAS-1 (DMAS plus an initial central plan), HMAS-2 (CMAS plus local LLM feedback; only acting robots join). Numbers (Table I, success %, mean of 40 runs; DMAS / HMAS-1 / CMAS / HMAS-2): BoxNet1 25.0 / 52.5 / 75.0 / 82.5; BoxNet2 0.0 / 7.5 / 27.5 / 57.5; Warehouse 0.0 / 5.0 / 15.0 / 62.5; BoxLift 52.5 / 67.5 / 90.0 / 100.0. Cost (normalized API calls) HMAS-2 vs CMAS: 4.62 vs 1.89 (BoxNet1), 14.90 vs 1.00 (BoxLift): HMAS-2 costs more. 3D (PyBullet, 3 and 6 arms): CMAS and HMAS-2 both 100%. Caveats: normalization is relative to the minimum across frameworks and ablations, so ratios are not comparable across tasks; Table I mixes success over all runs with metrics over successful runs only; Fig. 6 gives scaling as bars only. Venue not printed in the PDF.","COMBO (Zhang et al., ICLR 2025). Edge in this tree: child of CoELA (kind 2: CoELA reimplemented with oracle perception as an LLM-agent baseline). No kind 0/1 edge, so nothing here is inheritance inside the tree; it joins the line by topic (embodied cooperation, tree search) and by comparison. Own start: composable diffusion (Liu; Du), AVDC video model (Ko), VLP tree search (Du); it contrasts with Watch-And-Help and CoELA as work that does not model world dynamics. Tags: Mirsky ST2 (intent tracker) plus ST3 (tree search). Assumptions (Sec. 3.1, 6.1, App. A-C): Dec-POMDP; 336x336 RGBD egocentric views; shared goal; actions wait, pick up, place, cut; horizon 30; teammates are scripted; training data from random scripted rollouts (107k TDW-Game and 50k TDW-Cook videos); the world model was trained for about a day on 192 and 120 V100 GPUs; slow inference is a stated limitation. Method: world-state estimate from stitched RGBD plus diffusion inpainting; video diffusion with one text prompt per agent composed; LLaVA-1.5-7B LoRA sub-modules (Action Proposer, Intent Tracker, Outcome Evaluator); beam-style tree search P=3, B=3, D=3, replans every step. Numbers (Table 1, 20 episodes, success / avg steps of successes; TDW-Game cooperator 1): Recurrent WM 0; MAPPO 0; CoELA* (oracle perception) 0.90 / 18.4; LLaVA 0.55 / 28.4; COMBO without Intent Tracker 0.65 / 16.2; COMBO 1.00 / 17.5; Shared Belief* (oracle) 1.00 / 15.3. TDW-Cook COMBO 0.90 and 1.00 vs LLaVA 0.35 and 0.50. Real robot (App. D): 4/5. Caveats: only 20 episodes per cell; the world model fails 25% of 4-agent predictions (App. C.3). The value of k for the Intent Tracker is not stated.","Conformal MRP, i.e. S-ATLAS (Wang, He, Kantaros; WashU; arXiv v4 Nov 2024; venue RA-L 2025 taken from the file name; the PDF prints only the arXiv stamp). Edges: child of KnowNo (kind 0: builds on KnowNo&#x27;s conformal multiple-choice planner and help-seeking, generalising it to distributed teams). Child of Centralized vs not (kind 2: CMAS and DMAS as baselines, Appendix A). Cites RoCo and CoELA only inside a range of recent multi-robot LLM planners &#x27;without performance guarantees&#x27; (kind 2). It also uses the per-robot LLM action choice &#x27;as in&#x27; RoCo and Centralized vs not; I counted this as background, not inheritance. Problem: a robot team plans a natural-language mission that must succeed with probability at least 1 - alpha. Treating the team as one robot gives S^N joint choices (about 5.1e21 at N=15); the distributed version queries N times |S| options. Assumptions (Sec. II, III, Thm 4.2): error-free skills; calibration and test missions exchangeable, correct calibration plans written by hand; obstacle-free, known, static scene; homogeneous robots; faithful human; plans executed synchronously after construction. Method: sequential per-robot action choice, scores from one LLM query per option; nonconformity score of a sequence from its lowest confidence; local conformal set; one action left: act; else reshuffle order and retry, then ask a human. Numbers: Sec. V-A (110 scenarios x 30 calibration sequences, 50 repetitions, GPT-3.5): 94.59% at target 0.90, 96.57% at 0.95. Table I (N=2, help rate at 90%): Llama 2 S-ATLAS 29% vs centralized 88%; Llama 3 8% vs 30%. Table II (N=15, GPT-3.5, help off, plan accuracy): S-ATLAS 87.5, CMAS 25, DMAS 0; N=10: 95 / 60 / 5; N=3: 83.3 / 30.3 / 27.9; N=1: 92.5 / 37.2 / 37.2. With Llama models all methods are lower (Llama 3 at N=15 all 0%). Uncertain: the appendix text gives Case II CMAS/DMAS as 30.9/27.3 but Table II prints 30.3/27.9 (table used); plan correctness checked by hand by the authors; Table II compares plan quality, not the guarantee.","CoTS (Zu et al., CVPR 2025; the PDF prints &#x27;CVPR paper&#x27; but no year). Edges: child of Watch-And-Help (kind 1: C-WAH, extended from WAH, is a CoTS test environment); child of CoELA (kind 0: keeps most CoELA modules, replaces its planning module with MCTS-style collaborative tree search plus extended memory); child of RoCo (kind 2: compared as a baseline). CaPo is also a baseline but is not in this tree. Start: CoELA agents message each other but each picks its own next action with no long-term plan; RoCo and CaPo write one plan along one reasoning path, vulnerable to LLM randomness and frequent re-planning. Assumptions (Sec. 3-5, Conclusions): Markov game; decentralized agents each with an LLM; one planner and one critic (two agents in experiments); LLM-based reward (allocation and cost criteria scored 1-5, normalized to 0-1); perception, memory, execution largely borrowed from CoELA; depends on LLM strength (GPT-4 beats GPT-3.5). Method: tree nodes hold plan, critic feedback and reward; selection by UCT, expansion with n discussion paths, LLM evaluation, backpropagation; the plan evaluation module re-searches only if progress no longer fits the plan. Numbers (Table 1, TDW-MAT transport rate %): GPT-4 with oracle perception CoELA 85, RoCo 87, CaPo 89, CoTS 93 (+9.41%); without oracle CoELA 71, RoCo 72, CaPo 74, CoTS 83 (+16.90%). GPT-3.5 with oracle: CoELA 73, RoCo 77, CaPo 84, CoTS 82 (CaPo slightly ahead); without oracle 52, 55, 57, 59. Table 2 (C-WAH steps, GPT-4): visual CoELA 92, RoCo 89, CaPo 83, CoTS 81; symbolic 57, 57, 51, 49. Ablation (TDW-MAT avg): w/o reward 89, single-branch 88, w/o plan evaluation 90, full 93. Caveats: small test sets (24 and 10 tasks), no variance reported, gains are relative percentages; appendices (human-agent, cost) not in the PDF; the threshold value is not given. Guest link: CoTS evaluates on C-WAH (10 tasks, two per scenario), which extends Watch-And-Help; it reuses the environment, not WAH&#x27;s goal inference.","Benchmarks per paper (each paper&#x27;s own; numbers are not comparable across papers, partners or metrics). Watch-And-Help (guest): goal inference test-1 precision 0.85 / recall 0.96, test-2 0.68 / 0.64; random goals clash in 40% of episodes (Sec. 5.3). KnowNo: help reduced 10-24% vs baselines (paper&#x27;s summary); hardware tabletop help per step 0.58 vs 0.72 (Simple Set). CoELA: TDW-MAT transport rate 0.71 vs 0.43 (Table 1); C-WAH steps 57 vs 111 (Table 2). RoCo: success 0.44-0.95 over six tasks (Table 2; mean 0.75 is my average). Centralized vs not: Warehouse 62.5 vs 15.0 (CMAS), 0 (DMAS) (Table I). CoTS: TDW-MAT GPT-4 93 vs 85 (oracle perception), 83 vs 71 without. Conformal MRP: 94.59% at a 90% target, 96.57% at 95%. COMBO: 100% success in 17.5 steps, TDW-Game cooperator 1 (Table 1, 20 episodes). The shared benchmarks are CoELA and CoTS (TDW-MAT and C-WAH; C-WAH extends Watch-And-Help, whose own task is goal inference plus helping and is not comparable), and even there CoELA&#x27;s numbers in CoTS&#x27; tables are copied from the CoELA paper. Open points from the notes: simulated partners and small test sets (24, 10, 20 episodes); LLM cost; slow COMBO search; error-free skills (Conformal MRP). Uncertain: RoCo mean is mine; venue years from file names.","Benchmarks per paper (each paper&#x27;s own; numbers are not comparable across papers, partners or metrics). Watch-And-Help (guest): goal inference test-1 precision 0.85 / recall 0.96, test-2 0.68 / 0.64; random goals clash in 40% of episodes (Sec. 5.3). KnowNo: help reduced 10-24% vs baselines (paper&#x27;s summary); hardware tabletop help per step 0.58 vs 0.72 (Simple Set). CoELA: TDW-MAT transport rate 0.71 vs 0.43 (Table 1); C-WAH steps 57 vs 111 (Table 2). RoCo: success 0.44-0.95 over six tasks (Table 2; mean 0.75 is my average). Centralized vs not: Warehouse 62.5 vs 15.0 (CMAS), 0 (DMAS) (Table I). CoTS: TDW-MAT GPT-4 93 vs 85 (oracle perception), 83 vs 71 without. Conformal MRP: 94.59% at a 90% target, 96.57% at 95%. COMBO: 100% success in 17.5 steps, TDW-Game cooperator 1 (Table 1, 20 episodes). The shared benchmarks are CoELA and CoTS (TDW-MAT and C-WAH; C-WAH extends Watch-And-Help, whose own task is goal inference plus helping and is not comparable), and even there CoELA&#x27;s numbers in CoTS&#x27; tables are copied from the CoELA paper. Open points from the notes: simulated partners and small test sets (24, 10, 20 episodes); LLM cost; slow COMBO search; error-free skills (Conformal MRP). Uncertain: RoCo mean is mine; venue years from file names."]});
